WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.720
- Hey, guys, so we're in line

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.890
for our COVID-19 vaccines.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.540
- Vaccination 2021.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.240
- Shot number one.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.620
- [Narrator] More and
more people are lining up

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.300
to get their COVID-19 vaccines.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.750
Half of all US adults

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.150
have received at least one shot.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.527
- Hey, guys, we're on the way to get.

00:00:18.527 --> 00:00:20.030
- [Both] The second vaccine.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.860
- Pfizer, so we'll keep you
posted on our side effects.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.230
- How we're feeling after.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.063
- [Narrator] As they do,

00:00:26.063 --> 00:00:29.730
many are now also sharing
their side effects and some.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.980
- I had a tiny headache
and a tiny little red spot

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:32.920
on my arm.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.920
- [Narrator] Are more common than others.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.030
- I don't know if you guys can see it,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.940
there's a little bump right
above my left clavicle.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.080
- [Narrator] So what side
effects should people expect

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.750
after getting their shots?

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.300
And when is it important
to seek medical attention?

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.730
- I can't really lift my
arm like past my shoulder

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.763
but that's it.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.150
- [Narrator] Side effects like this,

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.610
pain and redness in the arm

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.040
where a person received their shot

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.440
are the most common.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.030
Dr. Krutika Kuppalli says
they can even be a good sign.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.690
- So the reason for the symptoms

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.590
is really because your immune system

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.690
is revving up to develop
those good antibodies

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.550
that you need to help
fight off the coronavirus

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.120
if you were to come into contact with it.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.210
- So basically, it's like a training

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.335
for your immune system.

00:01:15.335 --> 00:01:18.340
- Yeah, that's a really
good way to think about it.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.910
- [Narrator] Headaches,
chills, fever, nausea,

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.470
body aches and in some cases,
even vomiting or diarrhea

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.960
are normal, if a bit unpleasant.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.740
- I have been running to the bathroom.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.990
I feel like my body's shutting down.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.960
- [Narrator] People getting
the two-dose vaccines

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.330
from Pfizer and Moderna

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:38.590
may also feel different
from one dose to the next.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.870
Many report feeling worse
after the second shot.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:46.830
- Second COVID vaccine, the Pfizer shot,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.450
has me in the bed.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.030
- The second time you get the vaccine,

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.710
your body's already
experienced developing some

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:54.800
of the antibodies,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.530
so your antibody response

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.740
is gonna be much higher

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.200
and so that's why those
symptoms you develop

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.940
are gonna be a bit stronger.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.140
- [Narrator] But again,
this isn't everyone.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.930
Doctors still don't have enough data

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.550
to say one dose carries
more severe side effects

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:11.450
than the other.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.600
And whether the experience is different

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.000
for people who've had COVID.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.280
- I was getting a little bit concerned

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.260
but I figured this was just
an enlarged lymph node.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.400
- So some of the less common side effects

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.580
that we've seen of the vaccine

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.160
have been what we call lymphadenopathy

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.900
or enlarged lymph nodes.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.280
- [Narrator] Though rare,
this swelling tends to happen

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.430
on the same side of the
body as the injection.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.580
- It's a sign that your
immune system is working

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.900
and you might notice when you get a cough

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.928
or a cold, you get enlarged
lymph nodes in your neck.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.750
- [Narrator] Also rare are cases

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.120
where patients have reported heart issues,

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.840
temporary paralysis to
one side of the face

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.650
or serious allergic reactions,

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.530
resulting in rashes and
difficulty breathing.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.196
- This is one of the
reasons we have people wait

00:02:55.196 --> 00:02:58.048
after they get their vaccine.

00:02:58.048 --> 00:02:59.580
- [Nurse] Keep an eye on
you for 15 minutes, okay?

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.413
- [Woman] Okay.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.380
- [Nurse] Between now and then,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.150
if you feel anything outside ordinary,

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.180
please honk your horn.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.390
I'll come over, take a look

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:06.990
and make sure you guys are okay.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.310
- [Narrator] What's not normal

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.950
is having a runny nose,
cough or sore throat

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.250
after getting the vaccine.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.590
- If you had those symptoms,

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.320
I would be worried that you had some sort

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.340
of upper respiratory infection

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.280
or possibly even COVID.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.100
So I would recommend getting tested.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.970
- [Narrator] Typically,
any side effect starts

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.510
to get better within a day or two

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.900
of getting vaccinated.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.111
After that, Dr. Kuppalli recommends people

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.635
seek medical attention.

00:03:33.635 --> 00:03:36.590
- Also if they have things
like difficulty breathing,

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.780
shortness of breath, swelling,

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.200
things that would be
considered emergencies.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.343
- One of the more worrisome
adverse events reported recently

00:03:44.343 --> 00:03:48.160
is a very rare type of blood
clot several women experienced

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.760
after getting the Johnson
&amp; Johnson vaccine.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.300
More than seven million people

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.860
in the US have gotten this vaccine.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.980
- It really is one in a million people

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.540
that have had this event.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.410
- For now, US regulators

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.350
have paused distribution of J&amp;J's vaccine,

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.240
though Dr. Anthony Fauci
said he expects the vaccine

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.540
to return to use by the end of the week,

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.220
perhaps with additional
restrictions or warnings,

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.493
as was done in Europe.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.630
What are some of the things
that people should do

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:22.290
in order to dampen their side effects?

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.950
- I would try to schedule time

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.280
to just kind of have a mellow day, right?

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.870
So you don't know how the
vaccine's gonna affect you.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.090
- [Narrator] But Dr.
Kuppalli says don't worry

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.170
if you feel fine.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.120
The vaccine is still working.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.820
People over 55 typically
experience fewer side effects,

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.100
possibly because their immune
system gets weaker with age.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.390
- I don't want people to think oh,

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.493
if I don't have a side
effect, that's a bad thing.

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:48.537
People's bodies are different as well.

00:04:48.537 --> 00:04:50.900
- Don't be afraid to get the vaccine.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.520
Everyone reacts differently.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.730
Me and my sister did
not have any symptoms.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:55.563
It doesn't mean you won't

00:04:55.563 --> 00:04:57.490
but in the end, it's better than COVID.

